 ### [Mesh-based Sampling](6990-mesh-based-sampling.md)
-Uses mesh boundaries to localize surface evaluation, requiring only two samples per ray. It is efficient and applicable as a post-processing step to existing NeRF models.
+Mesh-based Sampling localizes surface evaluation by estimating the volume density or Signed Distance Field (SDF) to define an inner and outer mesh boundary, using learned features attached to mesh vertices to estimate radiance. It sets itself apart from sibling methods by requiring only two samples per ray, significantly improving runtime efficiency while remaining applicable as a post-processing step to any existing NeRF models. Choose it when real-time performance is critical and mesh geometry is available or can be approximated.
 
